# Loan Portfolio & Default Risk Analysis | SQL + Power BI

## Project Overview
This project analyzes loan portfolio data to identify default patterns and understand how loan grades, loan purposes, and borrower home ownership relate to loan defaults.

## Tools Used
- MySQL
- SQL
- Power BI
- DAX

## Key Metrics
- Total Loans: 28,638
- Defaulted Loans: 6,203
- Overall Default Rate: 21.66%
- Total Loan Amount: 277M (as displayed in the Power BI dashboard)

## Key Insights
- Loan grade G has the highest observed default rate at 98.31%, based on a small sample of 59 loans.
- Loan purpose and home ownership show different default rates.
- The overall default rate is 21.66%.

## Dashboard
The Power BI dashboard summarizes loan volume, default rate, loan grade, loan purpose, and home ownership.

![Loan Portfolio & Default Risk Dashboard](\Loan Portfolio & Default Risk dashboard.png)
## Disclaimer
This project is for educational and portfolio purposes. The observed relationships do not establish causation.
